      "math_academy_id": "q-80815",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=-3{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=8{b}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =7{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}-{b}_{3} \\\\  & =-{b}_{3}+7{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(2{b}_{3})-\\frac{7}{3}(-3{b}_{1})+\\frac{1}{4}(8{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{7}{3}{c}_{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
